---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How LogMyFlight handles your information and protects your flight records.">
  <article class="legal-page container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p><h1>Your data stays yours.</h1>
    <p class="notice"><strong>Before launch:</strong> Replace the developer identity, email address, effective date, and all TODO text, then have this starter policy reviewed for the countries where the app is offered.</p>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> {site.privacyEffectiveDate}</p>
    <p>This policy explains how {site.developerName} (“we”, “us”) handles information when you use LogMyFlight or visit this website.</p>
    <h2>Flight records and CloudKit</h2>
    <p>LogMyFlight stores and synchronizes your flight records using Apple CloudKit. This information is associated with your Apple account and stored in your private CloudKit database. We do not operate a separate LogMyFlight account service and cannot access the flight records in your private database.</p>
    <p>CloudKit is operated by Apple and is also subject to Apple’s privacy and iCloud terms.</p>
    <h2>Photos you select</h2>
    <p>LogMyFlight can receive the specific photos you choose to attach to a flight. Selecting a photo does not give the app unrestricted access to your entire photo library. Selected attachments form part of your app data and may synchronize with your records through CloudKit.</p>
    <h2>Analytics, advertising, and tracking</h2>
    <p>LogMyFlight and this website do not use third-party analytics, advertising SDKs, cross-site tracking, or advertising cookies. This website does not create user accounts or submit information through web forms.</p>
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Your records remain in your private CloudKit storage until you delete them through the app or Apple’s applicable iCloud controls. TODO: Confirm and document the released app’s precise deletion behavior, including whether deletion synchronizes across devices and how photo attachments are handled.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>LogMyFlight is a general-audience pilot utility and is not directed specifically to children. We do not knowingly operate a service that collects children’s personal information.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may revise this policy if the app’s features or data practices change. The effective date above will be updated when a revised policy is published.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or privacy requests can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>. Because we cannot access private CloudKit flight records, some data requests may need to be completed by you through the app or your Apple account.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

